      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For a source with five authors, the in-text citation in APA 7th edition is a bit simpler than you might think, as you'll use the first author's last name followed by \"et al.\" from the very first time you cite it. In Chicago style, however, you'll list all five authors the first time you cite it in your footnotes or bibliography, and then you can use a shortened form later on. It's a matter of choosing which style best suits your paper's overall needs, but remember to check your specific style guide guidelines!",
